WEBVTT

01:45.146 --> 01:47.315
<i>I've never seen a monster like this!</i>

01:48.566 --> 01:51.486
<i>The T. rex's teeth and tail.</i>

01:53.071 --> 01:56.407
<i>The Triceratops's feet and horns.</i>

01:57.283 --> 02:00.245
<i>The Pteranodon's wings and talons.</i>

02:01.663 --> 02:05.166
<i>The powers of three formidable foes,
all in one single animal.</i>

02:05.750 --> 02:08.461
<i>Each of them is already monster enough.</i>

02:09.754 --> 02:14.008
<i>Every last aspect of their strength
had been engraved into my body.</i>

02:17.262 --> 02:18.179
<i>Here it comes!</i>

02:19.264 --> 02:21.057
<i>The teeth, the horns,</i>

02:21.891 --> 02:24.435
<i>the talons, and the beak...</i>

02:25.603 --> 02:26.437
<i>All at once!</i>

02:28.523 --> 02:30.316
Baki's attacking!

02:30.942 --> 02:34.320
<i>"Genius" is the only way to describe
how he's handled things until now.</i>

02:34.404 --> 02:36.656
<i>But what will he do now?</i>

02:37.448 --> 02:41.828
<i>The actual weight of Baki is less
than even 1% of those dinosaurs.</i>

02:51.129 --> 02:53.298
<i>He may be the greatest
of the Cretaceous period,</i>

02:54.257 --> 02:57.051
<i>but he's a novice
when it comes to martial arts.</i>

02:59.387 --> 03:03.683
<i>Understandably, he mistook the pain
as that from a T-Rex's teeth.</i>

03:06.644 --> 03:08.188
<i>Now I get it.</i>

03:14.319 --> 03:15.153
Hey!

03:19.157 --> 03:21.701
<i>Baki, now you're going too far!</i>

03:23.453 --> 03:24.287
<i>That's right.</i>

03:25.413 --> 03:28.666
<i>No matter the rival,
when they meet, it's their first fight.</i>

03:29.167 --> 03:31.211
Does he plan on hitting him head-on?

03:31.794 --> 03:33.171
<i>Don't be too brash, Baki!</i>

03:35.131 --> 03:38.092
<i>But it wasn't his first time
having a first fight.</i>

03:44.807 --> 03:49.229
<i>The pose made when one is just about
to sprint at full speed is quite old.</i>

03:51.272 --> 03:53.274
<i>In the Olympics before World War II,</i>

03:53.358 --> 03:55.902
<i>there were still athletes
who used this form.</i>

03:57.528 --> 03:59.822
<i>The history
of the starting form for sprinting</i>

03:59.906 --> 04:03.034
<i>is also the history of how close
to horizontal a person can get.</i>

04:04.077 --> 04:05.703
<i>Ultimately, it looked like this.</i>

04:06.329 --> 04:11.417
<i>A consensus was reached
on this "crouch start" form for sprints.</i>

04:13.211 --> 04:15.797
By using this device called a starter,

04:16.547 --> 04:18.716
the body becomes
relatively more horizontal.

04:19.384 --> 04:22.345
<i>But naturally,
it's not totally horizontal.</i>

04:25.181 --> 04:29.686
<i>This day, someone has at last achieved
the first human horizontal start position.</i>

04:30.395 --> 04:32.105
<i>But this young man</i>

04:32.188 --> 04:35.358
<i>who achieved human's first fastest
and newest starting position</i>

04:35.441 --> 04:36.985
<i>was not a modern human.</i>

04:38.695 --> 04:42.907
<i>The time to contact with his opponent,
Baki Hanma, was less than one second.</i>

04:46.327 --> 04:49.580
<i>Later, the master of kung fu,
Sea King Retsu,</i>

04:49.664 --> 04:52.333
<i>spoke of that moment in this way.</i>

04:53.126 --> 04:54.502
<i>He said he "sensed" it.</i>

04:55.503 --> 04:58.172
<i>It will take time to describe with words,</i>

04:58.256 --> 05:00.925
<i>but I sensed many things in that instant.</i>

05:02.302 --> 05:03.303
<i>I thought, "I see."</i>

05:04.512 --> 05:08.266
<i>This is what Pickle used to do
in the ancient Cretaceous period.</i>

05:09.017 --> 05:11.436
<i>Sometimes he used the power of a tree,</i>

05:12.061 --> 05:14.022
<i>sometimes the power of a boulder.</i>

05:15.148 --> 05:18.484
<i>That's why he was able to stop
even a five-ton beast.</i>

05:19.652 --> 05:23.072
<i>At the same time,
I sensed this about Baki.</i>

05:23.948 --> 05:26.242
<i>Baki's weight was only around 70 kilos.</i>

05:27.035 --> 05:31.039
<i>But I, who weigh over 100 kilos,
couldn't stop Pickle's tackle,</i>

05:31.122 --> 05:33.124
<i>so how could he?</i>

05:33.875 --> 05:37.295
<i>What's more, Pickle had
an even greater advantage</i>

05:37.378 --> 05:40.089
<i>than when he started
on the ground against me.</i>

05:40.757 --> 05:43.885
<i>I thought, "I'm going to see
the end of this fight right here."</i>

05:45.803 --> 05:46.637
<i>What?</i>

05:46.721 --> 05:50.850
<i>How could I think so many things
in less than a second?</i>

05:53.895 --> 05:55.229
<i>Let's just say,</i>

05:55.813 --> 05:59.567
<i>you took a bite
of the most delectable curry and rice.</i>

06:00.568 --> 06:02.028
<i>Spicy. Salty.</i>

06:02.612 --> 06:04.572
<i>Sweet. A little sour.</i>

06:04.655 --> 06:07.909
<i>The aroma. The richness.
The texture of the ingredients.</i>

06:07.992 --> 06:10.078
<i>The spread of flavor. The spices.</i>

06:10.578 --> 06:12.914
<i>If you were to describe
the taste in detail,</i>

06:12.997 --> 06:14.916
<i>it would surely take you ten minutes.</i>

06:14.999 --> 06:19.003
<i>But it all happens in a mere ten seconds.</i>

06:19.087 --> 06:21.130
<i>Does that make sense?</i>

06:22.673 --> 06:26.761
<i>What surprised me was that Baki stopped.</i>

06:27.637 --> 06:32.266
<i>He dropped his stance and faced Pickle,
who was just standing there.</i>

06:32.350 --> 06:33.267
<i>That's right.</i>

06:34.602 --> 06:36.479
<i>He took the full force of him.</i>

06:37.146 --> 06:39.273
<i>There wasn't a moment for him to move.</i>

06:41.234 --> 06:42.235
<i>However,</i>

06:43.528 --> 06:45.530
<i>it was Pickle who flew off.</i>

06:46.114 --> 06:48.783
<i>No, he didn't bounce.</i>

06:49.992 --> 06:54.163
<i>He quite literally flew high
and far into the air.</i>

06:58.501 --> 07:01.337
Whoa! He... he flew!

07:02.964 --> 07:05.049
Did he throw him?

07:05.550 --> 07:06.426
I don't know.

07:07.760 --> 07:09.011
<i>That's no surprise.</i>

07:09.971 --> 07:14.725
<i>At that moment, Baki's only movement
was this. Like he was shooing away a fly.</i>

07:15.726 --> 07:19.188
<i>There's no move like that,
not even in old-style jujitsu or aikido.</i>

07:20.273 --> 07:24.193
<i>Though Pickle weighed over 200 kilos,
he was sent flying up to the ceiling</i>

07:24.277 --> 07:28.197
<i>by the casual flick of the hand
of a small man less than half his size.</i>

07:29.073 --> 07:31.200
Pickle is amazing.

07:32.410 --> 07:35.288
That guy, he's one hell of a man.

07:40.293 --> 07:43.713
Pretty impressive, King of the Cretaceous.

07:45.798 --> 07:49.844
Why? It was Baki who threw him!

07:49.927 --> 07:52.889
Why is Pickle so amazing
when he was the one who got thrown?

07:53.431 --> 07:55.766
I don't understand all the complexities.

07:55.850 --> 07:58.728
But there is something
that I do understand.

07:59.312 --> 08:02.398
The stronger the unleashed force,
the forward power,

08:02.482 --> 08:05.359
the more it is vulnerable
to force from the side.

08:06.194 --> 08:07.361
<i>When a gun is fired,</i>

08:08.154 --> 08:11.365
<i>a bullet that enters the belly
could exit from the side</i>

08:11.449 --> 08:13.367
<i>or through the shoulder.</i>

08:14.035 --> 08:17.497
<i>It can be affected by various factors
inside the soft stomach.</i>

08:18.289 --> 08:19.582
<i>In extreme cases,</i>

08:19.665 --> 08:23.753
<i>the single leaf of a houseplant
can bend a bullet's trajectory.</i>

08:24.337 --> 08:28.549
<i>If you think of Pickle as a bullet,
with as much force as a bullet,</i>

08:28.633 --> 08:32.637
<i>then even that light movement
could deflect him that far.</i>

08:32.720 --> 08:34.764
<i>That's what Hanayama said.</i>

08:35.473 --> 08:39.018
<i>What Hanayama said
reminded me of a fight.</i>

08:40.228 --> 08:43.981
<i>In 1964, in Miami, Florida, USA,</i>

08:45.149 --> 08:47.568
<i>there was the pro-boxing
heavyweight title match</i>

08:48.069 --> 08:50.613
<i>between Sonny Liston and Cassius Clay.</i>

08:51.739 --> 08:55.743
<i>The mighty right straight
that Liston threw was parried by Clay,</i>

08:55.826 --> 08:57.411
<i>successfully brushing it away.</i>

08:57.995 --> 09:02.416
<i>As a result, Liston's right shoulder
was seriously dislocated.</i>

09:03.167 --> 09:07.380
<i>It appeared to some experts that it was
because Clay's parrying was so powerful,</i>

09:07.463 --> 09:08.673
<i>but they're wrong.</i>

09:09.423 --> 09:13.010
<i>In fact, the force of Liston's punch
should be extolled for being so powerful</i>

09:13.094 --> 09:17.056
<i>that the parry dislocated his shoulder.</i>

09:30.152 --> 09:31.654
Oh, there.

09:40.788 --> 09:42.415
How do you like that?

09:42.498 --> 09:44.959
I had just enough to mark eight places.

09:47.295 --> 09:50.089
While you were cowering up there,

09:50.715 --> 09:52.883
this place has become my territory.

09:53.551 --> 09:56.220
What the heck?

09:56.304 --> 09:58.472
<i>I get it!</i>

10:13.446 --> 10:16.490
That's enough, I think.
That's enough of the tricks.

10:17.074 --> 10:22.121
T-Rex, Triceratops, Pteranodon,
I think I went too far with them.

10:22.788 --> 10:24.373
Back to basics.

10:25.041 --> 10:26.626
As fellow Homo sapiens...

10:30.755 --> 10:32.757
As humans, let's fight.

10:38.971 --> 10:40.765
<i>I wanna do this at least once.</i>

10:41.891 --> 10:42.767
<i>What a fool, huh?</i>

10:42.850 --> 10:45.019
<i>A head-to-head fight!</i>

10:45.686 --> 10:46.646
<i>To the ground--</i>

10:46.729 --> 10:50.066
<i>No! It's like I was smashed by the ground!</i>

10:50.650 --> 10:53.444
<i>I said I wanted a head-to-head fight.</i>

10:54.904 --> 10:58.282
<i>Was this what I expected?
Or more than I expected?</i>

11:16.175 --> 11:17.677
<i>Now I see.</i>

11:18.511 --> 11:21.138
<i>You really are strong.</i>

11:21.847 --> 11:23.432
<i>No doubt about it.</i>

11:26.394 --> 11:29.438
<i>Even when I block, it's like...</i>

11:31.899 --> 11:37.071
<i>the arms that I block with
have turned into weak spots!</i>

11:37.905 --> 11:39.573
<i>His strength is superhuman.</i>

11:40.783 --> 11:43.244
<i>This is the third time
I've seen the lights today.</i>

11:43.744 --> 11:45.079
<i>Superhuman strength?</i>

11:49.458 --> 11:52.086
<i>When I think of superhuman strength,
I think of him.</i>

11:52.795 --> 11:56.090
<i>Biscuit Oliva. Mr. Unchained.</i>

11:56.674 --> 11:59.927
<i>I'd love to see a scene like this.</i>

12:00.010 --> 12:02.346
<i>I'm sure he'd do it.</i>

12:02.930 --> 12:06.684
<i>A head-to-head fight.
Just like from the world of mythology.</i>

12:07.393 --> 12:08.728
<i>A head-to-head fight?</i>

12:09.770 --> 12:11.480
<i>Speaking of fights,</i>

12:12.148 --> 12:14.483
<i>that guy watching from over there,</i>

12:14.567 --> 12:15.776
<i>those fists.</i>

12:16.569 --> 12:19.822
<i>He's the same way. No cheap tricks.</i>

12:20.573 --> 12:23.784
<i>He'd do it for sure, from right in front.</i>

12:24.493 --> 12:25.494
<i>Right in front?</i>

12:25.578 --> 12:29.123
<i>If there's a "right in front,"
then what about "right in back"?</i>

12:29.790 --> 12:31.250
<i>That phrase doesn't exist.</i>

12:32.251 --> 12:35.129
<i>Speaking of backs, this is the real deal.</i>

12:35.212 --> 12:36.338
<i>Ogre!</i>

12:37.423 --> 12:39.842
<i>They both would use this stance.</i>

12:40.926 --> 12:43.763
<i>I wonder how that would end up.</i>

12:45.097 --> 12:47.391
<i>But, that's right,</i>

12:48.017 --> 12:49.894
<i>what I'm really interested in,</i>

12:49.977 --> 12:51.687
<i>what I really want to see is...</i>

12:52.688 --> 12:54.023
<i>how would Baki Hanma</i>

12:55.232 --> 12:57.526
<i>stop this guy?</i>

13:00.780 --> 13:02.865
<i>I've lived for 18 years.</i>

13:03.657 --> 13:05.534
<i>Mindfully, very cautiously.</i>

13:07.453 --> 13:08.287
<i>I have lived...</i>

13:10.748 --> 13:11.791
<i>to win.</i>

13:12.833 --> 13:16.545
<i>I've followed in the footsteps
of the most powerful being on Earth,</i>

13:16.629 --> 13:18.631
<i>Yujiro Hanma.</i>

13:19.131 --> 13:20.299
Why?

13:21.217 --> 13:23.677
<i>"Why?" you ask. Are you insane?</i>

13:23.761 --> 13:28.557
<i>Am I searching for a reason
to fight Yujiro Hanma?</i>

13:29.683 --> 13:32.394
<i>Wasn't it to get vengeance for my mother?`</i>

13:34.021 --> 13:36.232
<i>That's right. That was four years ago.</i>

13:38.567 --> 13:39.819
<i>Hatred...</i>

13:41.946 --> 13:42.988
<i>Hatred?</i>

13:44.573 --> 13:46.408
<i>Admiration...</i>

13:47.159 --> 13:50.830
<i>Don't be stupid! Why would I admire him?</i>

13:51.664 --> 13:52.915
<i>There's one thing...</i>

13:54.583 --> 13:56.669
<i>There's one thing that's very clear.</i>

13:57.962 --> 14:00.089
<i>Yujiro Hanma's strength.</i>

14:01.006 --> 14:02.800
<i>There's no denying it,</i>

14:02.883 --> 14:05.594
<i>every last inch of him is faultless.</i>

14:06.178 --> 14:07.304
<i>In a way,</i>

14:09.014 --> 14:10.850
<i>you could say it's trust.</i>

14:11.600 --> 14:13.352
<i>I've followed in his footsteps.</i>

14:14.395 --> 14:16.480
<i>I've equipped myself against those fists.</i>

14:17.189 --> 14:18.983
<i>I've pictured their speed.</i>

14:20.943 --> 14:24.363
<i>That's why I can dodge them.
I can dodge these.</i>

14:25.072 --> 14:28.868
<i>A single blow can lead to
serious trouble just by touching me.</i>

14:29.451 --> 14:30.369
<i>I can dodge it.</i>

14:31.078 --> 14:33.831
<i>Even more last-second. More effectively.</i>

14:34.456 --> 14:37.293
<i>He dodged them
with less and less time to spare.</i>

14:37.877 --> 14:39.336
<i>Closer to the last second.</i>

14:40.504 --> 14:44.008
<i>At first, his body twisted
with big movements.</i>

14:44.675 --> 14:48.637
<i>But then it brushed against his hair,
then grazed his skin.</i>

14:49.346 --> 14:53.142
<i>The closer he cut it, it was like...</i>

14:53.726 --> 14:56.520
<i>Rather than martial arts or fighting,</i>

14:57.062 --> 14:58.480
<i>it was more like a dance.</i>

14:58.564 --> 15:00.190
<i>That's right, like bullfighting.</i>

15:00.691 --> 15:02.401
<i>As if he were a matador.</i>

15:05.487 --> 15:07.281
<i>He had seen many kinds of speed.</i>

15:08.157 --> 15:11.368
<i>On land. In the water. In the air.</i>

15:12.953 --> 15:15.789
<i>And today, another new experience.</i>

15:20.794 --> 15:22.922
<i>A speed that defied the concept of speed.</i>

15:23.505 --> 15:27.301
<i>He didn't go through him,
he ghosted by him.</i>

15:28.677 --> 15:30.804
<i>At that moment, from Pickle's memory...</i>

15:33.182 --> 15:37.561
<i>At first, half in sport,
it was out of a desire for a snack.</i>

15:43.192 --> 15:45.277
<i>He learned they weren't so easy to catch.</i>

15:46.779 --> 15:48.697
<i>He got it! He was sure!</i>

15:51.909 --> 15:53.911
<i>He silently realized then</i>

15:54.620 --> 15:58.707
<i>that there were beings in this world
that could travel through his body.</i>

16:00.459 --> 16:04.088
<i>There was a renowned karate fighter
known as the father of fighting karate.</i>

16:04.171 --> 16:06.340
<i>Late in his life, he said,</i>

16:07.967 --> 16:10.010
<i>"I have dodged numerous thrusts."</i>

16:10.928 --> 16:12.638
<i>"I have received numerous kicks."</i>

16:13.430 --> 16:16.850
<i>"I've been attacked with numerous elbows,
knees, and headbutts."</i>

16:17.685 --> 16:21.939
<i>"Even with steel pipes,
thrown stones, and knives."</i>

16:22.982 --> 16:25.693
<i>"As close as possible, at the last second,</i>

16:26.694 --> 16:29.363
<i>only at the very last second,</i>

16:30.155 --> 16:31.532
<i>did I dodge them."</i>

16:33.200 --> 16:37.204
<i>Then during an ordinary practice,
he experienced an astonishing state.</i>

16:38.998 --> 16:40.624
<i>He said, "I passed through him."</i>

16:41.667 --> 16:44.128
<i>He said that he slipped
through his opponent.</i>

16:45.963 --> 16:48.132
<i>Of course, it was physically impossible.</i>

16:49.550 --> 16:51.593
<i>As a result of spending</i>

16:51.677 --> 16:54.722
<i>a mind-numbing amount of time
circling behind his opponents,</i>

16:55.723 --> 16:57.766
<i>his blocks, his defensive moves,</i>

16:58.350 --> 16:59.893
<i>his footwork...</i>

17:00.477 --> 17:02.896
<i>they were utterly stripped
of all wasted movement.</i>

17:03.522 --> 17:05.607
<i>He had transcended "circling opponents."</i>

17:06.567 --> 17:09.236
<i>He entered a state
of "passing through" them.</i>

17:15.576 --> 17:17.161
<i>Who is this male?</i>

17:19.413 --> 17:21.999
<i>Just how many tricks will he use?</i>

17:22.499 --> 17:28.672
Has he... Have Baki's fighting abilities
attained this high a level?

17:29.339 --> 17:30.716
<i>Could I do it?</i>

17:30.799 --> 17:33.302
<i>Can I replicate what he has done?</i>

17:36.930 --> 17:40.059
<i>The man crowned God of War, Doppo Orochi,</i>

17:40.726 --> 17:44.313
<i>the man called the walking embodiment
of fighting, Goki Shibukawa,</i>

17:45.522 --> 17:48.942
<i>and the man at the summit,
as the greatest active kung fu fighter,</i>

17:49.026 --> 17:50.819
<i>my teacher, Sea Emperor Kaku.</i>

17:50.903 --> 17:54.323
Could those three replicate this feat?

18:04.541 --> 18:06.585
<i>It was no surprise Pickle was astonished.</i>

18:07.503 --> 18:09.588
<i>The location of his elusive opponent</i>

18:11.381 --> 18:13.592
<i>was right up close to him.</i>

18:14.176 --> 18:17.096
<i>His left hand gripped an invisible saber</i>

18:17.596 --> 18:21.350
<i>that drove into the fighting bull's,
or rather, Pickle's weak spot...</i>

18:23.393 --> 18:25.104
<i>and penetrated deep.</i>

18:26.688 --> 18:30.734
<i>He had a feeling,
the coming pain would be great.</i>

18:31.860 --> 18:34.363
<i>Like when stubbing a toe
on the corner of a desk.</i>

18:35.239 --> 18:37.366
<i>Or when being struck hard
in the solar plexus.</i>

18:38.242 --> 18:42.287
<i>During the few moments we're granted
before the onset of actual pain,</i>

18:43.831 --> 18:48.460
<i>the brain has already predicted
the pain from the intensity of the blow.</i>

18:49.795 --> 18:53.382
<i>Immediately after, the pain hits
with the predicted intensity,</i>

18:53.465 --> 18:56.718
<i>and is as excruciating as predicted,
if not more.</i>

18:58.804 --> 19:01.849
<i>That is the period of preparation
that God granted us.</i>

19:03.725 --> 19:07.896
<i>He had two memories of this,
engraved into him from past tough battles.</i>

19:09.106 --> 19:11.650
<i>Here it comes!
The greatest wave of pain ever!</i>

19:11.733 --> 19:15.362
<i>The impact and the intensity
of the tremor tells him so.</i>

19:17.573 --> 19:18.407
<i>Here it is!</i>

19:19.783 --> 19:22.870
<i>Just as he imagined.
Even greater than he imagined.</i>

19:28.876 --> 19:31.503
That worked!

19:32.171 --> 19:33.172
Exactly.

19:33.797 --> 19:37.509
At any time and in every situation,
the crotch always works.

19:38.010 --> 19:43.557
Oh, but the balls are this tiny.
It causes this much pain?

19:43.640 --> 19:47.561
Just tiny balls? You are mistaken.

19:48.270 --> 19:51.565
This is certain.
The testicles are an internal organ.

19:51.648 --> 19:52.649
Really?

19:52.733 --> 19:53.567
They're fragile.

19:54.234 --> 19:56.445
<i>As a fetus, they're inside the body.</i>

19:57.070 --> 19:58.864
<i>They go out of the body to cool.</i>

19:59.907 --> 20:03.410
They're weak. There is nothing weaker.

20:04.036 --> 20:06.705
<i>They're as weak as the heart, the liver,</i>

20:07.456 --> 20:10.292
<i>the stomach, and the brain.</i>

20:11.919 --> 20:14.046
But those are protected

20:15.088 --> 20:18.967
<i>by thick muscle, fat, bones,</i>

20:19.551 --> 20:20.969
<i>and a sturdy skull.</i>

20:21.678 --> 20:23.138
However, the testicles,

20:23.222 --> 20:26.308
entrusted with the important task
of producing sperm,

20:26.391 --> 20:27.809
must be cooled.

20:28.310 --> 20:30.270
In order to accomplish this vital duty,

20:30.354 --> 20:33.982
they're forced outside the body,
wrapped in a mere single layer of skin.

20:34.900 --> 20:38.487
<i>They're exposed in this vulnerable state.</i>

20:39.905 --> 20:45.744
If the heart were dangling at your crotch
wrapped in a single layer of skin,

20:45.827 --> 20:49.039
it would be an incredible weakness
in times of battle.

20:49.122 --> 20:52.501
I could never leave the house.

20:55.879 --> 20:58.674
I guess it's over.

21:00.175 --> 21:01.009
No.

21:01.093 --> 21:02.427
No, it's not.

21:02.970 --> 21:04.263
What?

21:04.346 --> 21:07.975
Damn guy, he collapsed
with a good look on his face.

21:09.268 --> 21:11.979
Will you get back up,
or will you stay down?

21:13.105 --> 21:14.523
<i>The moment you're hit,</i>

21:15.023 --> 21:17.901
<i>the answer is instantly decided
within your heart.</i>

21:17.985 --> 21:21.071
<i>Do you think, "I'm beaten! Leave me be!"?</i>

21:22.114 --> 21:25.117
<i>Or "How dare he! I'll get him for this!"?</i>

21:26.118 --> 21:28.537
<i>Your expression in the moment of collapse...</i>

21:29.538 --> 21:35.043
<i>Any remainder of your will to fight,
will show in your expression.</i>

21:36.128 --> 21:39.298
<i>The look on Pickle's face a second ago...</i>

21:40.257 --> 21:42.843
Not only will he get back up,
but it seems that Baki

21:43.510 --> 21:46.430
has made Pickle's blood boil.

21:47.347 --> 21:49.182
<i>They were both trembling.</i>

21:50.058 --> 21:51.435
<i>With nervous tension.</i>

21:52.269 --> 21:53.186
<i>With anger.</i>

22:02.612 --> 22:03.739
<i>It's close.</i>

22:05.449 --> 22:07.451
<i>This fight's been a long one.</i>

22:08.327 --> 22:09.953
<i>But the finale is close.</i>

22:11.830 --> 22:12.956
<i>This face.</i>

22:14.416 --> 22:16.043
<i>This stance.</i>

22:17.085 --> 22:19.129
<i>This is his final form.</i>
